# RLL-1 local automation — {{REPOSITORY}}

This is a thin repository adapter for Common Engineering Relay V3.1 RLL-1.

Required Common basis: `{{REQUIRED_COMMON_BASIS}}`.

## Architecture

```text
Antigravity schedule sidecar
  -> repository PowerShell wrapper
  -> Common V3.1 rll_worker.py
  -> deterministic git + gh transport
  -> one agy -p engineering run
  -> GitHub evidence
```

## Install smoke mode

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/install-rll1-antigravity-sidecar.ps1 `
  -CommonRoot "C:\path\to\Common" `
  -PilotIssue <issue>
```

## Authentication and Antigravity permission

Authenticate GitHub CLI once with `gh auth login --web` and verify `gh auth status`. RLL expects GitHub CLI to use the operating-system credential store. Do not set `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN` for the sidecar and never copy an OAuth/PAT into sidecar JSON or Antigravity settings.

For Antigravity CLI, use the documented `/config` → Tool Permission setting. Do not add undocumented wildcard grant entries such as `command(*)` or `write_file(*)`. Unattended host-backed execution may require the documented `always-proceed` mode; because it is broad, use a dedicated least-privileged OS account/workspace. Prefer `proceed-in-sandbox` where the task can truly run without host filesystem/network access.

The smoke pilot must be an OPEN bounded issue that has not already reached `REVIEW_READY` or `CANCELLED`. Never reopen completed engineering work just to reuse it as the RLL pilot.

## Enable execution

After smoke review:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/install-rll1-antigravity-sidecar.ps1 `
  -CommonRoot "C:\path\to\Common" `
  -PilotIssue <same-open-pilot> `
  -EnableExecution
```

Use `BRANCH_RESUME` only for a governed source-write branch.
Use `EXACT_HEAD_EVIDENCE` for read-only immutable-head execution.

Execution enablement does not add `rll-ready` again; it resumes the smoke-established RLL state.

Never use transport state as engineering PASS/FAIL.
Never use RLL to infer merge/release authority.
